75173>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75173>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75173>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75173>>>// string information.
75173>>>//
75173>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75173>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75173>>>//       End_Procedure
75173>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75173>>>//                        bar title
75173>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75173>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75173>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75173>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75173>>>//                        is used.
75173>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75173>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75173>>>//
75173>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75173>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75173>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75173>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75173>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75173>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75173>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75173>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75173>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75173>>>//   end_procedure
75173>>>//   // end of file.
75173>>>
