79187>>>>>    
79187>>>>>    // Attempt to make this as intuitive as possible. You cannot invoke this when a
79187>>>>>    // report is active. If a report is not finished, you cannot do this.
79187>>>>>    // If a report is finsihed it may or may not have a viewer present.
79187>>>>>    // If a viewer is not present, we will clear the exising report (making the assumption
79187>>>>>    // that a modeless viewer was closed and the report will not be invoked again). If a viewer
79187>>>>>    // is active, we will pass this through to the winprint object which will show an error
79187>>>>>    
79187>>>>>    Function DFPrintSetupDialog Returns Boolean// invoke printer setup dialog
79189>>>>>        Integer iStatus
79189>>>>>        Boolean bActiveViewer bOk
79189>>>>>        // we must have printers installed for this to work
79189>>>>>        Get ArePrintersInstalled to bOk
79190>>>>>        If not bOk Begin
79192>>>>>            Error DFERR_WINPRINT C_$NoInstalledPrinters
79193>>>>>>
79193>>>>>        End
79193>>>>>>
79193>>>>>        Else Begin
79194>>>>>            Get DocumentStatus to iStatus
79195>>>>>            If (iStatus=dsFinished) Begin
79197>>>>>                Get IsViewerActive to bActiveViewer
79198>>>>>                If not bActiveViewer Begin
79200>>>>>                    Send DfClearDoc
79201>>>>>                End
79201>>>>>>
79201>>>>>            End
79201>>>>>>
79201>>>>>            // the winprint object will generate an error if the status is not dsNotStarted.
79201>>>>>            // we want those errors
79201>>>>>            Get DFPrintSetupDialog of (phoWinPrint(Self)) to bOk
79202>>>>>        End
79202>>>>>>
79202>>>>>        Function_Return bOk
79203>>>>>    End_Function
79204>>>>>    
79204>>>>>    // It is better to use DFPrintSetupDialog which tells you if the dialog was canceled
